#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.11"
# dependencies = [
#     "httpx>=0.27",
#     "capabilities-contract>=0.50,<1",
# ]
# ///
"""signoz — agent-first CLI for SigNoz telemetry and configuration APIs.

It supports SigNoz Cloud and self-hosted Community/Enterprise installations.
Agent-invoked: run `signoz help` to reload this menu and `signoz help <verb>`
for one verb's whole contract, on demand. The management/query API and OTLP
ingestion are deliberately separate: SIGNOZ_API_KEY reads or manages SigNoz,
while SIGNOZ_INGESTION_KEY only authenticates Cloud telemetry ingestion.
Self-hosted ingestion normally has no key. Run `signoz guide connections` for
the exact deployment matrix, and `signoz doctor` first to prove a deployment
answers.

CONNECTIONS
An explicit connections registry is required, even for one deployment. A
connection is one SigNoz deployment: its management URL and API key, and
optionally its OTLP endpoint, Cloud ingestion key, proxy headers, environment
scope and dimension map. Secrets are names of env vars, never literal values.
The keys, their compatibility aliases, the registry shape and how a
connection is selected are on `signoz help connections`; `signoz connections`
reports how each value resolves, locally.

A connection's environment or scope filter scopes every data query unless the
query overrides it, as each query verb's page says. Connection dimensions map
the logical agent, call and room names to project-specific fields. Outside any
project, connections and doctor are machine reads; every other verb that
needs a connection is refused there.

COMMANDS
  Deployment
  signoz version                 server version and edition; the endpoint is public
  signoz ingestion               a secret-free OTLP environment plan for the deployment

  Discovery
  signoz services                services observed in a time window
  signoz metrics                 the metric catalog: type, unit, last seen
  signoz fields keys             the queryable field names of one signal
  signoz fields values           the observed values of one field

  Logs and traces
  signoz logs search             raw log rows matching shortcut filters and an expression
  signoz traces search           raw spans matching shortcut filters and an expression
  signoz trace <trace-id>        the spans of one trace
  signoz call <call-id>          correlated logs and traces for one call
  signoz agent <agent-id>        correlated logs and traces for one agent
  signoz query <file|->          a complete Query Builder v5 request, as given

  Configuration
  signoz dashboards [<id>]       list dashboards, or fetch one
  signoz alerts                  current Alertmanager instances
  signoz rules [<id>]            alert-rule definitions, v1 or v2 by server version
  signoz views [<id>]            saved Explorer views, or one
  signoz channels [<id>]         notification channels, or one

  Escape hatch
  signoz api <METHOD> <path>     a documented API not covered above; WRITE unless GET

I/O CONTRACT
  Success is JSON on stdout. Failure is {"error": {"code","message","hint"?,
  "status"?}} on stderr, with nothing on stdout; the exit code carries the
  category.

EXIT CODES
  0 success · 2 missing/rejected API credentials · 3 not found ·
  4 project/write policy refusal (ask the user; never lift it yourself) ·
  5 network/server/protocol failure · 6 invalid input.
"""

